3. THE MODEL, ITS BANDS AND THE SEARCH
   MODELED: three nodes, FE_OUT (the front end injects), R11 + L11, VBUS20, R16 + L16, CH_ACN (the charger draws); each part
     ESR + jwESL + 1/(jwC); 60 harmonics by a 4096-point midpoint DFT; the FE's mean square at its worst (VIN, fsw) plus the
     charger's at its worst (VBAT, fch), per part (the two are not synchronised)
   RECORD (r4-decisions.md section 6 B3, the lost analysis's bands; each INFERRED there, no maker figure held):
     polymer ESL 1.50 to 3.50 nH in 41 steps; ceramic effective C 4.000 to 7.000 uF in 25 steps (the 10u 50V X7R 1210 at 20 V: no
     DC-bias curve for it is held); ceramic ESL 0.80 / 1.15 / 1.50 nH, ESR 2 / 5 mOhm; L16 5 / 20 nH; L11 1 / 3 / 5 nH (the record gives 1 to 5 nH;
     three points, ASSUMPTION, from its 332,100 sets); can C x0.8 / 1.0 / 1.2 (MAKER +-20 %), ESR x0.3 / 1.0 / 2.0 (1.0 the sheet's maximum, 2.0 its
     endurance limit, 0.3 a good part, the lost analysis's least-damping corner)
   the grids: VIN_RAW 9, 10, 12, 13.8, 16, 24, 36 V (RECORD, REQ-015's 9 to 36 V); fsw 11 points over the carried row; VBAT 10 points over 10.0 to 16.8 V
     (RECORD; 16.8 V the VBAT rail's v_work, 4S full); fch 7 points over each SLUSE66A row; the spacing of fsw, VBAT, fch and L11
     even (ASSUMPTION: the record gives the counts and the ends only)
   ASSUMPTION (the predecessor's values; no maker figure held): C190 and C191 at 20 and 50 mOhm, 0.5 nH; the ceramic bank's 0.4
     mOhm and the light load 0.25 A in the loop; the loop's corners (Q 0.4 / 0.8, gm x0.8 / 1.2, cans C x0.8 / 1.2, ESR x0.3 / 2.0)
   the spread (RECORD): one can at the corner's ESR, its siblings at s times it; 'worst can' is the larger of the two
   SESSION search: stage 1 bounds every set of the coarse grid (ESL indices 0,10,20,30,40, C indices 0,8,16,24, every other band at all its
     corners); stage 2 climbs the 6 best-bounded sets (one per corner of the other bands) on the dense grid; stage 3 bounds the
     whole dense ESL x C slice at the best and evaluates every set whose bound exceeds it (validation and evaluation runs)

