6. THE RE-SIZE (SESSION). The sharing basis: the cans' ESR within 2:1 (read at 100 kHz before fitting) AND each can's branch
   within 0.5 nH and 0.5 mOhm of every other's (a layout rule: a 10 mm VBUS20 pour 0.2 mm over its plane is about 25 pH/mm, so
   0.5 nH is a 20 mm path difference; 0.5 mOhm two squares of 2 oz copper), both against the one can with the lowest ESR and the
   shortest branch. The rule: every can at most 2.8 A less the consistency tolerance scaled to the current (0.0035 A per A) at every
   spread, on the larger of a full search (at the binding 2:1 spread on the decision grids, VBAT every 0.2 V, fSW every 2.5 kHz,
   the charger every 5 kHz; at the others on the record's) and its maximum converged on 4b's grids; the groups screened in
   order of the change at the 2:1 spread on the record's grids;
   the first group with a bank that meets the rule gives the bank, the lowest worst can within it
